Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 33 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENSIVELY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  LYPMH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 26 OF 28 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   HIGH LEVEL 2    METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor cells do not transgress the lymph node capsules  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 97 at 17 04     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labelled with patients name  unit number  and   left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fibroadipose tissue fragment  The specimen margins are inked as follows  Yellow   superior  red   lateral  green   medial  blue   inferior  black   deep  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm well circumscribed  hard  tan   pink mass  0 5cm from the deep margin and 1 0cm from the superior margin  A representative portion is frozen and saved frozen  Section code AandB  Deep margin C  Superior margin DandE  Mass  representative section  br report_end  , Unchecked.
