GIN  UNORIENTED   EXCISION  FOCAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  ASSOCIATED WITH MINUTE FOCUS OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  INVOLVING 2 OF 4 BLOCKS  SPANNING UP TO REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE FINAL MARGIN  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue with two localization wires in place  A short black stitch designates the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  The inferior margin is inked black  the superior blue  the medial green  and the lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm indurated gray white poorly delineated region which abuts the inferior margin and comes to 0 4cm of the superior  0 4cm of the anterior  0 6cm of the lateral  1 0cm of the medial  and 1 1cm of the anterior margin  A silver metal clip is noted along the anterior aspect of the area  and the area is between the two localization wires  The remaining mammary tissue is dense gray white and fibrous  Representative sections are submitted from posterior to anterior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the tissue bearing the silver metal clip as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the firm area as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  posterior right margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm unoriented tan yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue  The unoriented specimen is serially sectioned  and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  medial lateral margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue  There is a suture along one aspect designating the new margin  The new sutured margin is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned  and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan yellow lobulated portion of lymph node bearing fatty tissue  Multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 1cm in maximum dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four whole possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four whole possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two whole possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node  Gross Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Bracht