re developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 28     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     THE REST OF THE AXILLARY TISSUE HAS BEEN EXAMINED  NINE ADDITIONAL LYMPH NODES ARE PRESENT  VARYING IN SIZE FROM  0 1 CM  TO REMOVED_DATE CM  NO EVIDENCE OF FIBROSED FORMER NODES PRESENT  REMOVED_DATE NODES CONTAINS A SINGLE FOCUS OF METASTATIC CARCINOMA MEASURING  0 1 CM   WITH EVIDENCE OF SLIGHT EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  THE INVOLVED LYMPH NODE IS REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE CM  IN SIZE  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 09 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x x 4 0cm mastectomy specimen with an axillary tail  Short stitch demarcates the superior portion of the specimen and a long stitch demarcates the axillary tail  A skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with a central  1 0cm in length retraction  is also present  Approximately 2 5cm lateral to the skin ellipse  in the same horizontal plane  is an irregular shaped region of fibrous tissue  with a central area that has an increased firmness and grittiness  compared to its surrounding tissue  This area measures approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  and is approximately greater than 2 0cm from the posterior  closest  margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma has numerous ill defined fibrous areas throughout  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  SECTION CODE  A D  nodular area with increased firmness  E  closest  posterior  margin  F  representative section of fibrous tissue surrounding central firm area  G  fibrous tissue in the inferior anterior medial portion of the specimen  approximately 4 0cm from skin ellipse  H  fibrous tissue in the mid lateral portion of the specimen  greater than 2 0cm from the posterior margin  I M  lymph nodes with the largest lymph nodes  bivalved and submitted as cassette I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and count 27  sentinel node  blue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of fatty tissue  with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm lymph node  Lymph node is submitted in entirety as cassette N  Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  GRAY OR 40 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Alphonse Taghian  M D  David Bent Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY WITH AXILLARY CONTENTS PART B  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL NODE  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 18 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM   EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  LYMPH NODE  LEFT BREAST   METASTATIC CARCINOMA INVOLVING ONE OF ONE INTRAPARENCHYMAL LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 05                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a firm nodule abutting the edge  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm hard  gritty  tan yellow mass involving multiple inked resection margins  A representative portion of the mass is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Representative sections of the lesion with margins are submitted in A through J  Gross Description by  Timothy R  Quinn  MD Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING AND IN  SITU CARCINOMA WITH FEATURES OF LOBULAR TYPE  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 56 CLINICAL DATA  Non palpable right breast cancer on sterotactic core from outside hospital                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT    ADDITIONAL MARGIN   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 17 OF 17 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 19                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  number only is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast with a localizing needle and accompanying specimen X ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white stellate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm lesion extending to within 0 5cm of the closest inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Sections of mass are submitted in cassettes A B  Representative sections of breast  submitted in cassettes C E  A portion of the lesion is taken by Dr  Deutch  Received in two container  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm aggregate mass of adipose tissue and lymph nodes  Lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes F through Q  Labeled  additional margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE unoriented piece of breast tissue  Sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes R through T  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PARTIAL MASTECTOMY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART C  ROGHT BREAST  ADDITIONAL MARGIN   report_end  , Unchecked.
