Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  12 AUG 98 at 15 24 CLINICAL DATA  60 y o  female with left breast ca biopsy REMOVED_DATE  invasive ca  had been on HRT now stopped                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  SINGLE FOCUS SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT AT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERO SUPERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS AND PRESENT AT THE ANTERO SUPERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL SUPERFICIAL LATERAL MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL DEEP MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SLIGHT ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE FINAL DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Dr  Koerner has reviewed slides P R and agrees with this interpretation  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN TWO OF ELEVEN LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  17 AUG 98 at 17 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 AUG 98 at 09 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast lump  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of breast tissue with a localizing wire entering the lateral superficial portion  The specimen is entirely inked black and posterior surface is overinked blue  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm  white stellate mass with fibrous extensions located  0 5cm from the posterior margin  and abutting the superficial margin  Sectioning through the remaining breast parenchyma reveals rubbery white fibrous tissue with a small amount of adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted  Section code  A B  Mass to closest posterior margin  inked blue  and closest superficial margin  inked red   C  Section of remaining breast parenchyma overinked in red  D  Representative section from remaining breast parenchyma  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final superficial lateral margin  is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  One side of the specimen is inked black  the opposing side is inked blue  Sectioning reveals predominantly adipose tissue with a small amount of soft gray white fibrous tissue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of firm gray white fibrous tissue  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm cystic space  Representative sections are submitted  SEction code  E  Sections from firm fibrous area F G  Sections including cyst H  Section from remaining tissue  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm aggregate of adipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  The cut surfaces of the lymph node range from tan pink to yellow and fatty  Representative sections are submitted in cassette I L  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additonal left breast tissue suture marks final deep margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a suture on one side designating the final deep margin  This deep margin is inked black and the opposing margin is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal predominantly gray white rubbery fibrous tissue admixed with a small amount of fibroadipose tissue  No lesions or masses are grossly appreciated  Sections to include all the fibrous tissue are submitted in M V  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA ABUTTING THE SUPERFICIAL MARGIN  AND  0 5 CM FROM DEEP MARGIN  O R  Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERFICIAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISIO PART B  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART D  BREAST   LEFT 