Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 AUG 03 ACCESSIONED ON  11 AUG 03 at 12 58 CLINICAL DATA  Left spindle cell neoplasm  status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy without significant response                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  HIGH GRADE PHYLLODES TUMOR  17 CM  WITH MASSIVE STROMAL OVERGROWTH AND EXTENSIVE NECROSIS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Tumor is broadly present less than a fraction of a millimeter from the deep margin and extends to 0 12cm from the anterior margin  It abuts but does not invade the overlying skin  Lymphovascular invasion is not seen  Although rare tumor cells are positive for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the classic biphasic pattern of a phyllodes tumor is focally identified  The tumor cells also show focal positivity for S 100  but are negative for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam REMOVED_DATE  desmin  myoglobin  myogenin  and myo REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Receptor studies will be reported in an addendum  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 14 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  15 AUG 03 at 18 11                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block G   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  Rare tumor cells stain faintly for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  20 AUG 03 at 14 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast stitch at 12 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 15 3cm mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE attached skin with nipple  The areola is 4 3cm in diameter and the nipple is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The skin of the specimen is mottled overlying a mass which largely replaces the breast parenchyma  The mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm  The mass is tan and fleshy with a large central cystic area containing necrotic debris and bloody fluid  There are several polypoid projections into the cyst  The mass abuts the posterior margin and overlying skin anteriorly  The tumor grossly abuts the anterior surgical margin as well  The posterior surgical margin is inked black and the anterior surgical margin is inked blue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Tumor to skin  C F  Tumor to deep margin  G  Tumor to posterior and anterior margins  H J  Polypoid excrescences  K P  Solid tumor  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty tissue  Out of this tissue are 15 firm nodular fragments of tan soft tissue ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Seven nodules were sectioned and individually submitted entirely in cassettes Q W  Eight smaller nodules were submitted four to a cassette in cassettes X and Y  Resident  CHRISTOPHER M  WILLIAM  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Alphonse Taghian  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  MODI