 number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm lobular fibrofatty breast tissue with two needle localization wires and a short stitch indicating the superior aspect and a long stitch indicating the lateral aspect  The specimen is inked as follows  medial aspect green  lateral aspect yellow  superior aspect blue and inferior aspect black  The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior  Cross section reveals predominately soft yellow lobulated fat interspersed with a small amount of firm white fibrous tissue  There are multiple foci of hemorrhage corresponding the needle localization wires  There is a 0 1cm spherical tan blue cyst which is 0 5cm from the lateral margin  No other discrete lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from the anterior margin to the posterior margin with the cyst in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the area corresponding to the calcifications in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of fibrous areas in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm yellow pink fibrofatty tissue  with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm white skin ellipse  There is short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  There are four undesignated localization wires in place  This specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  and lateral yellow  The specimen is sequentially sectioned from inferior to superior to reveal a cut surface consisting of yellow lobulated adipose tissue and white dense fibrous tissue  with multiple cysts filled with bloody serous fluid  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan finely granular firm area within the tissue  which abuts the medial margin  comes to within 0 2cm of the posterior margin  comes to within 1 2cm of anterior margin  and is greater than 2cm to the remainder margins  This firm area surrounds a clip and is adjacent to a wire  No additional lesions or masses are appreciated  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from inferior to superior  with area of clip within blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of biopsy cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections away from biopsy cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and   right breast  is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular lobule of fibrofatty breast tissue  Cross section reveals predominately soft yellow lobulated fat interspersed with a small amount of dense to soft white fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Holly A Brunner  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Holly A Brunner  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT DEEP   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 21 CLINICAL DATA  Right mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY SITE WITH FOCAL ACUTE INFLAMMATION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15 08                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a right mastectomy specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5cm  oriented with a long stitch   lateral  and a short stitch   superior   The entire specimen is inked black  over inked blue on the anterior side  The skin ellipse shows a well healed scar  linear  1 5cm   localized laterally from an otherwise unremarkable nipple areolar complex  The specimen is sectioned from superior to inferior  A biopsy cavity surrounded by fibrinous tissue is found underneath the skin scar  The cavity measures 1 4cm in its greatest diameter  is 0 5cm from the posterior resection margin  and is hard in consistency  The cavity has a smooth lining and contains some yellow material  Fibrous tissue surrounds the cavity  The rest of the parenchyma is unremarkable  SECTION CODES  A B  biopsy cavity and surrounding tissue  C  cavity area  spanning the entire cross section of the specimen  D  cavity area from anterior to posterior  E  lateral to cavity  F  medial to the cavity  G  more medial than the previous section  posterior margin  H  area localized more anteriorly from the cavity  posterior margin  lateral  2 0cm from the inferior resection margin  I  1 0cm from the cavity  0 5cm from the inferior resection margin  2 7cm from the lateral resection margin  J  section 