Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 MAY 04 ACCESSIONED ON  11 MAY 04 at 13 09 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma  status post chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH FEATURES OF CHEMOTHERAPY EFFECT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH FEATURES OF CHEMOTHERAPY EFFECT  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH CALCIFICATIONS  PROFIFERATIVE FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  0 1 CM DEPOSIT  WITH FOCAL EXTRANODAL EXTENSION IN 1 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Multiple scattered microscopic foci up to 1 CM  Grade  cannot assess due to superimposed chemotherapy effect  Lymphatic vessel invasion  absent  Blood vessel invasion  absent  Margin of invasive carcinoma  more than REMOVED_DATE CM from margins  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  within and beyond region of region of invasive tumor  Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  cannot assess due to chemotherapy effect  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  more than REMOVED_DATE CM from margins  Stains for receptors  performed on prior specimens  Note  Careful gross evaluation of the axillary tail revealed multiple potential lymph nodes which were all submitted for microscopic evaluation however all but 2  which were lymph nodes  represented dense fibrous nodular tissue  Submission of additional axillary tissue did not reveal additional lymph nodes  Diagnosis by  JOSEPH T  RABBAN  M D   M P H  Signed On  18 MAY 04 at 07 56                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REM