 margin  and 10cm from the posterior margin  The remaining parenchyma shows focal areas of fibrosis  No lymph nodes are identified in the axillary aspect of the specimen  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Prior biopsy site  fibrotic area  representative sections   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodules  0 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm   adjacent to the biopsy site  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Parenchyma between the two nodules in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the calcified nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Calcified nodule and adjacent breast parenchyma  with the calcified nodule submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  following decalcification   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant  fibrotic parenchyma  representative sections to the posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant  fibrotic area  representative section   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of biopsy site sampled in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional hard nodule adjacent to biopsy site  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary contents   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm  3 large lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  5 x 1 x 0 3cm  and REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 9cm are identified  Smaller candidate lymph nodes  ranging from 0 2cm to 0 9cm in greatest dimension are also identified  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Large fatty lymph node  2 9cm    sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Large fatty lymph node  5cm    sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Large fatty lymph node  4 5cm    sectioned and entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple intact candidate lymph nodes  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remaining fibroadipo