as hemorrhage at the periphery  The mass is 1 0cm from the inferior margin  grossly abuts the medial margin  0 8cm from the posterior margin  1 0cm from the anterior margin  0 5cm from the lateral margin  and greater than 2cm from the superior margin  This mass grossly corresponds to the third  most inferior  needle localization wire  The most superior needle localization wire corresponds to an area of blue inked yellow adipose tissue but no discrete mass  The middle needle localization wire corresponds to an ill defined area consisting of punctate yellow white lesions extending for an overall distance of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A D  Mass designated by the most inferior localization wire  from inferior to superior  E G  Area designated by the middle localization wire  H J  Area designated by the superior localization wire  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  left axillary sentinel node   are two pieces of fat  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  One of the specimens contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm tan nodule  This entire nodule is frozen as FX 1  The second portion of fat is frozen as FX 2  Representative sections are submitted as follows  K  FX 1  L  FX 2  M  Remaining fat  not frozen  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved deep   is an non oriented piece of fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes N O  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved inferior   is an non oriented piece of fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  which is submitted entirely in cassette P  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final saved anterior medial 