Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 19 06 CLINICAL DATA  86 year old female with a history of right breast mastectomy in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   now with invasive carcinoma of left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HEALING BIOPSY TRACK  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Invasion of blood vessels and lymphatics is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 39     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR KERATIN LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THE LYMPH NODES DO NOT CONTAIN KERATIN POSITIVE CARCINOMA CELLS  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast with axillary nodes  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 14 5cm skin ellipse attached  On the surface of the skin is an inverted nipple  with apparently no areolar complex  Superior and lateral to the nipple is a hard white  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm nodule that comes to within 3 0cm of the skin  Sections of the nodule are submitted in cassettes A  B  and C  Away from the nodule is an area with a mottled white pink and yellow surface  It is not firm  Sections submitted in cassette D  The rest of the breast tissue is unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes E and F  Lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes G through K  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART   LEFT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
