Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 19 14 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  MICROSCOPIC FOCI  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Residual carcinoma is not identified  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 54                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm segment of breast tissue  partially lined by a triangular shaped  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm unremarkable skin ellipse containing 1 0cm in greatest dimension retracted nipple  The nipple is 1 5cm to one tip of the skin ellipse  and 1 0cm to the two lateral margins  The same skin tip is marked by a double black suture  There is a 3 8cm linear well healed biopsy scar away from the suture marked tip  3 0cm from the nipple and 1 8cm from the parallel skin margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm irregularly shaped  tan white to yellow firm nodule  approximately 1 0cm from surrounding soft tissue surface  anterior margin   1 5cm from the areas corresponding to the biopsy scar  1 0cm from the nipple and approaching to the deep resection margin  The firm nodule consists of multiple cystic areas without gross necrosis  The remaining tissue consists of unremarkable yellow adipose tissue admixed with patchy breast parenchyma and fibrous tissue without grossly identifiable lesion  Representative sections surrounding the nodule and deep margin are submitted in cassettes A through J  Additional sections from other areas are submitted in K  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART   RIGHT SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
