Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 36 CLINICAL DATA  49 year old woman for an incisional biopsy of a breast nodule                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE   PRESENT ON 2 OF 3 SLIDES   HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS AND EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No blood or lymphatic vascular invasion is identified  Invasion of the stroma is not seen  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 58 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain diffusely for CEA and focally for Leu 7  The tumor cells do not stain for chromogranin  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 03     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Invasive carcinoma in not present in the sections stained for hormone receptor proteins  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  are two fibrous fragments of breast tissue  2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The tissue is inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue as well as a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lobulated tan white mass present at the inked margin  Specimen submitted in its entirety in cassettes A through C  with the nodular area in A  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX  1  LEFT BREAST   NO LESIONS GROSSLY DEFINITIVE FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Adult Medicine  CNT  126 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  ELIZABETH A RAFFERTY  M D  Resident  Colleen A Lamb  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 48 year old woman who presents with right breast mass  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  HIGH GRADE  WITH SYNCYTIAL GROWTH PATTERN AND PROMINENT LYMPHOPLASMACYTIC INFILTRATE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Sections of the core biopsy reveal an invasive carcinoma involving five of five core biopsies  The tumor grows in large fused nests with a distinctly syncytial growth pattern  There is a dense inflammatory infiltrate composed predominately of lymphocytes and plasma present  The tumor cells are large and markedly pleomorphic with ill defined cytoplasm and have enlarged hyperchromatic vesicular nuclei with marked nuclear contour irregularities and prominent macronucleoli  Scattered mitotic figures including atypical mitoses are readily identified  The morphologic findings are those of a high grade ductal carcinoma and suggest the possibility of a medullary carcinoma  Definite classification is deferred to the excision  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or co